I can update documentation for nixpkgs later. nix flake is an alternative to it that could be used while we get nixpks PR approved. also works as an option for people who would like to have more control on which version of mcp-hub use (to do not depend on version packaged in nixpkgs)

for maintenance i can create a github action that updates the nix.flake (it will also help to validate mcp-hub server mounts)
The nix.flake file needs to be update each time package-lock file changes or version of the package.json change

body:
Is there any way to pass env via system env vars?, for example:

```
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "brave-search": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-brave-search"],
      "env": {
        "BRAVE_API_KEY": "<secret>"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

I want mcp server to use the secret that i already set via env var but not hardcoding in the mcpservers.json.

